    qrCodeBadgeText: 'ASI Monument of National Importance / Soma Tirtha Multi-Faith Complex',
    audioTranscriptEn:
      'Om Namah Shivaya! Walk out across the sweeping grey granite whaleback of Ranipur-Jharial in Bolangir—celebrated in the Vamana Purana as Soma Tirtha. Few places in all South Asia display such fearless spiritual harmony on a single sheet of living rock. Around the reflective waters of Soma Sagar stand more than fifty medieval temples alongside rock-cut footprints of Tantric Siddhas and a serene seated Buddha, while a ninth-century Sanskrit lintel inside Someshwara Temple still speaks my name: Acharya Gaganasiva of the Mattamayura Shaiva order.\n\nClimb to the highest granite crown and enter our fifty-foot roofless circle of the Sixty-Four Yoginis. Unlike coastal Hirapur, here every Yogini dances in mid-whirl—many bearing fierce, mystical heads of lioness, mare, elephant, and serpent—all orbiting a four-pillared central pavilion where three-headed, eight-armed Nataraja dances the rhythm of creation. Then turn northward toward the sky: rising seventy-five feet in glowing crimson terracotta is Indralath, one of India’s tallest and finest tenth-century carved brick temples, sculpted with Narasimha and Krishna.',
